IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`

-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1 -- piece dg5, layer 1.
-- Sections 223 (vacancies and newly created directorships), 225 (contested election of directors; proceedings to determine validity),
-- 226 (appointment of a custodian or receiver on deadlock or for other cause) and 227 (powers of the Court in elections of directors).
--
-- The source is the plain-text rendering de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt of the Delaware Code Online (through 85 Del. Laws, c. 550).
-- It is not the official text. `-- src:N | ...` is line N of that file; an ellipsis means the line goes on.
--
-- Whatever the text hands to the Court of Chancery ("may hear and determine", "if the Court determines", "may appoint") is an input answered conditionally:
-- the rules say who may apply and on what ground, and what follows if the Court so orders. They never decide for the Court.
-- Sections 211 and 215 (elections, piece dg4), 291 (receivers, piece dg9) and 352(a)(2) (piece dg10) are out of range; section 114(b)(2) takes
-- sections 222 and 231 out of the stockholder-to-member reading, and none of sections 223 to 227 is on that list.

§ `Section 223 -- vacancies and newly created directorships`

-- src:901 | (a) Unless otherwise provided in the certificate of incorporation or bylaws:
-- src:902 | (1) Vacancies and newly created directorships resulting from any increase in the authorized number of directors elected by all of the stockholders having the right to vote as a single class may be filled by a majority of the directors then in office, although less than a quorum, or by a sole remaining director;
-- src:903 | (2) Whenever the holders of any class or classes of stock or series thereof are entitled to elect 1 or more directors by the certificate of incorporation, vacancies and newly created directorships of such class or classes or series may be filled by a majority of the directors elected by such class or classes or series thereof then in office, or by a sole remaining director so elected.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 223(a) (src:901-903)
DECLARE `dg5 s 223(a) Directorship to be filled` IS ONE OF
    `a directorship of a director elected by all the stockholders having the right to vote as a single class`
    `a directorship of a director elected by the holders of a class or series who are entitled to elect 1 or more directors by the certificate of incorporation`
    `a directorship of some other kind that section 223(a) does not describe`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 223(a) (src:901-903)
DECLARE `dg5 s 223(a) Filling of a vacancy by the directors` HAS
    `the directorship being filled under section 223(a)`                                                  IS A `dg5 s 223(a) Directorship to be filled`
    `where a provision otherwise providing is made`                     IS A `Where a provision is made`
    `the filling complies with the provision otherwise providing`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the number of directors in office who may fill the directorship`    IS A NUMBER
    `the number of those directors who vote to fill it, or act as the sole remaining director` IS A NUMBER

-- "Unless otherwise provided in the certificate of incorporation or bylaws": the displaceable default of the core. A resolution of the board does not displace it.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 223(a) (src:901)
GIVEN w IS A `Where a provision is made`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 223 the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws provide otherwise` w MEANS
    CONSIDER w
    WHEN `in the certificate of incorporation` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `in the bylaws` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `in a resolution of the board of directors` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `in none of these` THEN FALSE

-- By a majority of the directors then in office (although less than a quorum), or by a sole remaining director; for a directorship of a class or series,
-- by a majority of the directors elected by that class or series then in office, or by a sole remaining director so elected.
-- NOTHING: a directorship of another kind, or counts that cannot be a vote. When the certificate or bylaws provide otherwise, the answer is whether that provision was complied with.
-- src:902 | (1) Vacancies and newly created directorships resulting from any increase in the authorized number of directors elected by all of the stockholders having the right to vote as a single class may be filled by a majority of the directors then in office, although less than a quorum, or by a sole remaining director;
-- src:903 | (2) Whenever the holders of any class or classes of stock or series thereof are entitled to elect 1 or more directors by the certificate of incorporation, vacancies and newly created directorships of such class or classes or series may be filled by a majority of the directors elected by such class or classes or series thereof then in office, or by a sole remaining director so elected.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 223(a) (src:902-903)
GIVEN f IS A `dg5 s 223(a) Filling of a vacancy by the directors`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 223(a) the directors have filled the vacancy in the manner the section provides` f MEANS
    IF `s 223 the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws provide otherwise` (f's `where a provision otherwise providing is made`)
    THEN JUST (f's `the filling complies with the provision otherwise providing`)
    ELSE CONSIDER f's `the directorship being filled under section 223(a)`
         WHEN `a directorship of a director elected by all the stockholders having the right to vote as a single class` THEN
             CONSIDER `the vote carries` (`a majority of` `the directors then in office`) (f's `the number of those directors who vote to fill it, or act as the sole remaining director`) (f's `the number of directors in office who may fill the directorship`)
             WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
             WHEN JUST b  THEN JUST (b OR ((f's `the number of directors in office who may fill the directorship`) EQUALS 1 AND (f's `the number of those directors who vote to fill it, or act as the sole remaining director`) EQUALS 1))
         WHEN `a directorship of a director elected by the holders of a class or series who are entitled to elect 1 or more directors by the certificate of incorporation` THEN
             CONSIDER `the vote carries` (`a majority of` (`another base named in the provision` "the directors elected by such class or classes or series then in office")) (f's `the number of those directors who vote to fill it, or act as the sole remaining director`) (f's `the number of directors in office who may fill the directorship`)
             WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
             WHEN JUST b  THEN JUST (b OR ((f's `the number of directors in office who may fill the directorship`) EQUALS 1 AND (f's `the number of those directors who vote to fill it, or act as the sole remaining director`) EQUALS 1))
         WHEN `a directorship of some other kind that section 223(a) does not describe` THEN NOTHING

-- src:904 | If at any time, by reason of death or resignation or other cause, a corporation should have no directors in office, then any officer or any stockholder or an executor, administrator, trustee or guardian of a stockholder, or other fiduciary entrusted with like responsibility for the person or estate of a stockholder, may call a special meeting of stockholders in accordance with the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws, or may apply to the Court of Chancery for a decree summarily ordering an election as provided in § 211 or § 215 of this title.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 223(a) (src:904)
DECLARE `dg5 s 223(a) Person who may act when there are no directors` IS ONE OF
    `an officer of the corporation, acting where there are no directors`
    `a stockholder, acting where there are no directors`
    `an executor, administrator, trustee or guardian of a stockholder, or other fiduciary entrusted with like responsibility for the person or estate of a stockholder`
    `someone else, who may not act where there are no directors`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 223(a) (src:904)
GIVEN p IS A `dg5 s 223(a) Person who may act when there are no directors`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 223(a) the person is one of those who may act when there are no directors` p MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `an officer of the corporation, acting where there are no directors` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a stockholder, acting where there are no directors` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an executor, administrator, trustee or guardian of a stockholder, or other fiduciary entrusted with like responsibility for the person or estate of a stockholder` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `someone else, who may not act where there are no directors` THEN FALSE

-- "may call a special meeting of stockholders in accordance with the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws".
@ref 8 Del. C. § 223(a) (src:904)
GIVEN p IS A `dg5 s 223(a) Person who may act when there are no directors`
      `the corporation has no directors in office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the call is in accordance with the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 223(a) the person may call a special meeting of stockholders` p `the corporation has no directors in office` `the call is in accordance with the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws` MEANS
        `s 223(a) the person is one of those who may act when there are no directors` p
    AND `the corporation has no directors in office`
    AND `the call is in accordance with the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws`

-- "or may apply to the Court of Chancery for a decree summarily ordering an election as provided in § 211 or § 215" (out of range: sections 211 and 215, piece dg4).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 223(a) (src:904)
GIVEN p IS A `dg5 s 223(a) Person who may act when there are no directors`
      `the corporation has no directors in office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 223(a) the person may apply to the Court of Chancery for a decree summarily ordering an election` p `the corporation has no directors in office` MEANS
        `s 223(a) the person is one of those who may act when there are no directors` p
    AND `the corporation has no directors in office`

-- A director chosen under subsection (a) on a classified board holds office until the next election of the class for which the director was chosen
-- (and until a successor is elected and qualified). NOTHING: the directors are not divided into classes, so the subsection says nothing (section 141(b), piece dg2, governs).
-- src:905 | (b) In the case of a corporation the directors of which are divided into classes, any directors chosen under subsection (a) of this section shall hold office until the next election of the class for which such directors shall have been chosen, and until their successors shall be elected and qualified.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 223(b) (src:905)
GIVEN `the directors of the corporation are divided into classes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the next election of the class for which the director was chosen` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 223(b) the date until which the director chosen holds office, and until a successor is elected and qualified` `the directors of the corporation are divided into classes` `the date of the next election of the class for which the director was chosen` MEANS
    IF `the directors of the corporation are divided into classes`
    THEN JUST `the date of the next election of the class for which the director was chosen`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- out of range: section 141 (piece dg2)
-- "holding at least 10 percent of the voting stock at the time outstanding having the right to vote for such directors": 10 percent is reached.
-- "the directors then in office shall constitute less than a majority of the whole board (as constituted immediately prior to any such increase)": not more than half.
-- The Court's order ("may, upon application ... summarily order an election") is its own judgment: this rule answers only whether the stockholders may apply.
-- NOTHING: the counts cannot be a vote.
-- src:906 | (c) If, at the time of filling any vacancy or any newly created directorship, the directors then in office shall constitute less than a majority of the whole board (as constituted immediately prior to any such increase), the Court of Chancery may, upon application of any stockholder or stockholders holding at least 10 percent of the voting stock at the time outstanding having the right to vote for such directors, summarily order an election to be held to fill any such vacancies or newly created directorships, or to replace the directors chosen by the directors then in office as aforesaid, which election shall be governed by § 211 or § 215 of this title as far as applicable.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 223(c) (src:906)
GIVEN `the number of directors in office when the vacancy or newly created directorship is filled` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of directors of the whole board as constituted immediately before any increase` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of votes of the voting stock held by the applicants` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of votes of the voting stock at the time outstanding having the right to vote for such directors` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 223(c) the stockholders may apply to the Court of Chancery to order an election` `the number of directors in office when the vacancy or newly created directorship is filled` `the number of directors of the whole board as constituted immediately before any increase` `the number of votes of the voting stock held by the applicants` `the number of votes of the voting stock at the time outstanding having the right to vote for such directors` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the vote carries` (`a majority of` `the whole board`) `the number of directors in office when the vacancy or newly created directorship is filled` `the number of directors of the whole board as constituted immediately before any increase`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST inOffice THEN
        CONSIDER `the vote carries` (`at least` (10%) `of` (`another base named in the provision` "the voting stock at the time outstanding having the right to vote for such directors")) `the number of votes of the voting stock held by the applicants` `the number of votes of the voting stock at the time outstanding having the right to vote for such directors`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST ten THEN JUST ((NOT inOffice) AND ten)

-- "a majority of the directors then in office, including those who have so resigned, shall have power to fill such vacancy or vacancies, the vote thereon to take effect when such resignation or resignations shall become effective".
-- Unless the certificate or bylaws provide otherwise.
-- src:907 | (d) Unless otherwise provided in the certificate of incorporation or bylaws, when 1 or more directors shall resign from the board, effective at a future date, a majority of the directors then in office, including those who have so resigned, shall have power to fill such vacancy or vacancies, the vote thereon to take effect when such resignation or resignations shall become effective, and each director so chosen shall hold office as provided in this section in the filling of other vacancies.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 223(d) (src:907)
GIVEN w IS A `Where a provision is made`
      `the filling complies with the provision otherwise providing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of directors in office, including those who have resigned effective at a future date` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of those directors who vote to fill the vacancy` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 223(d) the directors may fill the vacancy before the resignation takes effect` w `the filling complies with the provision otherwise providing` `the number of directors in office, including those who have resigned effective at a future date` `the number of those directors who vote to fill the vacancy` MEANS
    IF `s 223 the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws provide otherwise` w
    THEN JUST `the filling complies with the provision otherwise providing`
    ELSE `the vote carries` (`a majority of` `the directors then in office`) `the number of those directors who vote to fill the vacancy` `the number of directors in office, including those who have resigned effective at a future date`

-- src:907 | the vote thereon to take effect when such resignation or resignations shall become effective, and each director so chosen shall hold office as provided in this section in the filling of other vacancies.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 223(d) (src:907)
GIVEN `the date on which the resignation becomes effective` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 223(d) the date on which the vote filling the vacancy takes effect` `the date on which the resignation becomes effective` MEANS
    `the date on which the resignation becomes effective`

§ `Section 225 -- contested elections and proceedings to determine validity`

-- src:915 | (a) Upon application of any stockholder or director, or any officer whose title to office is contested, the Court of Chancery may hear and determine the validity of any election, appointment, removal or resignation of any director or officer of any corporation, and the right of any person to hold or continue to hold such office, and, in case any such office is claimed by more than 1 person, may determine the person entitled thereto; and to that end make such order or decree in any such case as may be just and proper, with power to enforce the production of any books, papers and records of the corporation relating to the issue. In case it should be determined that no valid election has been held, the Court of Chancery may order an election to be held in accordance with § 211 or § 215 of this title. In any such application, service of copies of the application upon the registered agent of the corporation shall be deemed to be service upon the corporation and upon the person whose title to office is contested and upon the person, if any, claiming such office; and the registered agent shall forward immediately a copy of the application to the corporation and to the person whose title to office is contested and to the person, if any, claiming such office, in a postpaid, sealed, registered letter addressed to such corporation and such person at their post-office addresses last known to the registered agent or furnished to the registered agent by the applicant stockholder. The Court may make such order respecting further or other notice of such application as it deems proper under the circumstances.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 225(a) (src:915)
DECLARE `dg5 s 225 Applicant to the Court of Chancery` IS ONE OF
    `a stockholder, applying under section 225`
    `a director, applying under section 225`
    `an officer of the corporation whose title to office is contested`
    `the corporation itself, applying under section 225`
    `someone else, who may not apply under section 225`

-- Subsection (a): any stockholder or director, or any officer whose title to office is contested.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 225(a) (src:915)
GIVEN a IS A `dg5 s 225 Applicant to the Court of Chancery`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 225(a) the applicant may apply to the Court of Chancery to determine the validity of an election, appointment, removal or resignation` a MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN `a stockholder, applying under section 225` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a director, applying under section 225` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an officer of the corporation whose title to office is contested` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the corporation itself, applying under section 225` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `someone else, who may not apply under section 225` THEN FALSE

-- Subsection (b): any stockholder, or the corporation itself, on the result of any vote of stockholders on matters other than the election of directors or officers.
-- src:916 | Upon application of any stockholder or upon application of the corporation itself, the Court of Chancery may hear and determine the result of any vote of stockholders upon matters other than the election of directors or officers. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 225(b) (src:916)
GIVEN a IS A `dg5 s 225 Applicant to the Court of Chancery`
      `the vote was upon a matter other than the election of directors or officers` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 225(b) the applicant may apply to the Court of Chancery to determine the result of the vote of stockholders` a `the vote was upon a matter other than the election of directors or officers` MEANS
        `the vote was upon a matter other than the election of directors or officers`
    AND (   a EQUALS `a stockholder, applying under section 225`
         OR a EQUALS `the corporation itself, applying under section 225`)

-- src:916 | and no other party need be joined in order for the Court to adjudicate the result of the vote. The Court may make such order respecting notice of the application as it deems proper under the circumstances.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 225(b) (src:916)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 225(b) another party must be joined for the Court to adjudicate the result of the vote` MEANS
    FALSE

DECLARE `dg5 s 225 Kind of application` IS ONE OF
    `an application under subsection (a) of section 225 about an election, appointment, removal or resignation`
    `an application under subsection (b) of section 225 about the result of a vote of stockholders`
    `an application under subsection (c) of section 225 to remove a director`

DECLARE `dg5 s 225 Party to an application` IS ONE OF
    `the corporation as party to the application`
    `the person whose title to office is contested`
    `the person, if any, claiming the office`
    `the director or directors whose removal is sought`
    `another person, who is not a party named in section 225`

-- Service of the application upon the registered agent is deemed service upon the corporation, and under (a) upon the person whose title to office is contested and the person, if any, claiming the office;
-- under (c) upon the director or directors whose removal is sought; under (b) upon the corporation only.
-- src:915 | In any such application, service of copies of the application upon the registered agent of the corporation shall be deemed to be service upon the corporation and upon the person whose title to office is contested and upon the person, if any, claiming such office …
-- src:916 | Service of the application upon the registered agent of the corporation shall be deemed to be service upon the corporation …
-- src:917 | In any such application, service of copies of the application upon the registered agent of the corporation shall be deemed to be service upon the corporation and upon the director or directors whose removal is sought …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 225(a) (src:915); § 225(b) (src:916); § 225(c) (src:917)
GIVEN app IS A `dg5 s 225 Kind of application`
      party IS A `dg5 s 225 Party to an application`
      `the application was served upon the registered agent of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 225 service upon the registered agent is deemed service upon the party` app party `the application was served upon the registered agent of the corporation` MEANS
        `the application was served upon the registered agent of the corporation`
    AND (CONSIDER app
         WHEN `an application under subsection (a) of section 225 about an election, appointment, removal or resignation` THEN
             (   party EQUALS `the corporation as party to the application`
              OR party EQUALS `the person whose title to office is contested`
              OR party EQUALS `the person, if any, claiming the office`)
         WHEN `an application under subsection (b) of section 225 about the result of a vote of stockholders` THEN
             party EQUALS `the corporation as party to the application`
         WHEN `an application under subsection (c) of section 225 to remove a director` THEN
             (   party EQUALS `the corporation as party to the application`
              OR party EQUALS `the director or directors whose removal is sought`))

-- The registered agent "shall forward immediately a copy of the application ... in a postpaid, sealed, registered letter" (subsections (a) and (c)).
-- Subsection (b) states no such duty: NOTHING.
-- src:915 | and the registered agent shall forward immediately a copy of the application to the corporation and to the person whose title to office is contested and to the person, if any, claiming such office, in a postpaid, sealed, registered letter addressed to such corporation and such person at their post-office addresses last known to the registered agent or furnished to the registered agent by the applicant stockholder. …
-- src:917 | and the registered agent shall forward immediately a copy of the application to the corporation and to such director or directors, in a postpaid, sealed, registered letter addressed to such corporation and such director or directors at their post office addresses last known to the registered agent or furnished to the registered agent by the applicant. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 225(a) (src:915); § 225(c) (src:917)
GIVEN app IS A `dg5 s 225 Kind of application`
      `the application was served upon the registered agent of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 225 the registered agent must forward a copy of the application immediately` app `the application was served upon the registered agent of the corporation` MEANS
    CONSIDER app
    WHEN `an application under subsection (a) of section 225 about an election, appointment, removal or resignation` THEN JUST `the application was served upon the registered agent of the corporation`
    WHEN `an application under subsection (b) of section 225 about the result of a vote of stockholders` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `an application under subsection (c) of section 225 to remove a director` THEN JUST `the application was served upon the registered agent of the corporation`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 225(a) (src:915); § 225(c) (src:917)
GIVEN `the copy was sent in a postpaid, sealed, registered letter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the letter was addressed to the post-office address last known to the registered agent or furnished to the registered agent by the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 225 the registered agent has forwarded the copy in the manner the section requires` `the copy was sent in a postpaid, sealed, registered letter` `the letter was addressed to the post-office address last known to the registered agent or furnished to the registered agent by the applicant` MEANS
        `the copy was sent in a postpaid, sealed, registered letter`
    AND `the letter was addressed to the post-office address last known to the registered agent or furnished to the registered agent by the applicant`

-- src:915 | the Court of Chancery may hear and determine the validity of any election, appointment, removal or resignation of any director or officer of any corporation, and the right of any person to hold or continue to hold such office, and, in case any such office is claimed by more than 1 person, may determine the person entitled thereto; and to that end make such order or decree in any such case as may be just and proper, with power to enforce the production of any books, papers and records of the corporation relating to the issue. …
-- src:915 | In case it should be determined that no valid election has been held, the Court of Chancery may order an election to be held in accordance with § 211 or § 215 of this title. …
-- src:915 | The Court may make such order respecting further or other notice of such application as it deems proper under the circumstances.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 225(a) (src:915)
DECLARE `dg5 s 225(a) Power of the Court of Chancery on an application` IS ONE OF
    `to hear and determine the validity of an election, appointment, removal or resignation and the right of any person to hold or continue to hold the office`
    `to determine the person entitled to an office claimed by more than 1 person`
    `to make such order or decree as may be just and proper, with power to enforce the production of books, papers and records of the corporation relating to the issue`
    `to order an election to be held in accordance with section 211 or section 215`
    `to make such order respecting further or other notice of the application as it deems proper`

-- Each power belongs to the Court; the rule says only on what footing it can be exercised on the person's application.
-- Ordering an election needs the Court's determination "that no valid election has been held"; the claim of two persons to one office is needed for the determination between them.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 225(a) (src:915)
GIVEN power IS A `dg5 s 225(a) Power of the Court of Chancery on an application`
      `an application under subsection (a) is before the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court determines that no valid election has been held` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the office is claimed by more than 1 person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 225(a) the Court of Chancery may exercise the power on the application` power `an application under subsection (a) is before the Court` `the Court determines that no valid election has been held` `the office is claimed by more than 1 person` MEANS
        `an application under subsection (a) is before the Court`
    AND (CONSIDER power
         WHEN `to hear and determine the validity of an election, appointment, removal or resignation and the right of any person to hold or continue to hold the office` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `to determine the person entitled to an office claimed by more than 1 person` THEN `the office is claimed by more than 1 person`
         WHEN `to make such order or decree as may be just and proper, with power to enforce the production of books, papers and records of the corporation relating to the issue` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `to order an election to be held in accordance with section 211 or section 215` THEN `the Court determines that no valid election has been held`
         WHEN `to make such order respecting further or other notice of the application as it deems proper` THEN TRUE)

-- Subsection (c): removal of a director by the Court. The Court's two determinations (no good faith; removal necessary to avoid irreparable harm) are inputs: "if the Court determines".
-- src:917 | If 1 or more directors has been convicted of a felony in connection with the duties of such director or directors to the corporation, or if there has been a prior judgment on the merits by a court of competent jurisdiction that 1 or more directors has committed a breach of the duty of loyalty in connection with the duties of such director or directors to that corporation, then, upon application by the corporation, or derivatively in the right of the corporation by any stockholder, in a subsequent action brought for such purpose, the Court of Chancery may remove from office such director or directors if the Court determines that the director or directors did not act in good faith in performing the acts resulting in the prior conviction or judgment and judicial removal is necessary to avoid irreparable harm to the corporation. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 225(c) (src:917)
DECLARE `dg5 s 225(c) Application to remove a director` HAS
    `the director has been convicted of a felony in connection with the duties of the director to the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `there has been a prior judgment on the merits by a court of competent jurisdiction that the director has committed a breach of the duty of loyalty in connection with the duties of the director to the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the application is made by the corporation, or derivatively in the right of the corporation by a stockholder` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the application is made in a subsequent action brought for such purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Court determines that the director did not act in good faith in performing the acts resulting in the prior conviction or judgment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Court determines that judicial removal is necessary to avoid irreparable harm to the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref 8 Del. C. § 225(c) (src:917)
GIVEN r IS A `dg5 s 225(c) Application to remove a director`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 225(c) the Court of Chancery may remove the director from office` r MEANS
        (   r's `the director has been convicted of a felony in connection with the duties of the director to the corporation`
         OR r's `there has been a prior judgment on the merits by a court of competent jurisdiction that the director has committed a breach of the duty of loyalty in connection with the duties of the director to the corporation`)
    AND r's `the application is made by the corporation, or derivatively in the right of the corporation by a stockholder`
    AND r's `the application is made in a subsequent action brought for such purpose`
    AND r's `the Court determines that the director did not act in good faith in performing the acts resulting in the prior conviction or judgment`
    AND r's `the Court determines that judicial removal is necessary to avoid irreparable harm to the corporation`

§ `Section 226 -- a custodian or receiver on deadlock or for other cause`

-- src:921 | (a) The Court of Chancery, upon application of any stockholder, may appoint 1 or more persons to be custodians, and, if the corporation is insolvent, to be receivers, of and for any corporation when:
-- src:922 | (1) At any meeting held for the election of directors the stockholders are so divided that they have failed to elect successors to directors whose terms have expired or would have expired upon qualification of their successors; or
-- src:923 | (2) The business of the corporation is suffering or is threatened with irreparable injury because the directors are so divided respecting the management of the affairs of the corporation that the required vote for action by the board of directors cannot be obtained and the stockholders are unable to terminate this division; or
-- src:924 | (3) The corporation has abandoned its business and has failed within a reasonable time to take steps to dissolve, liquidate or distribute its assets.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 226(a) (src:921-924)
DECLARE `dg5 s 226(a) Application for a custodian` HAS
    `the applicant is a stockholder`                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `at a meeting held for the election of directors the stockholders are so divided that they have failed to elect successors to directors whose terms have expired or would have expired upon qualification of their successors` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the business of the corporation is suffering or is threatened with irreparable injury because the directors are so divided that the required vote for action by the board cannot be obtained` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the stockholders are unable to terminate that division`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the corporation has abandoned its business`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the corporation has failed within a reasonable time to take steps to dissolve, liquidate or distribute its assets` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the corporation is insolvent`                                                IS A BOOLEAN

-- Each of the three grounds is alternative ("or"). Ground (2) needs both the injury from the division and that the stockholders cannot end it.
-- Ground (3) needs both the abandonment and the failure within a reasonable time (whether the time is reasonable is the Court's judgment, taken as a fact).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 226(a) (src:921-924)
GIVEN a IS A `dg5 s 226(a) Application for a custodian`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 226(a) a ground exists on which the Court of Chancery may appoint a custodian` a MEANS
        a's `the applicant is a stockholder`
    AND (   a's `at a meeting held for the election of directors the stockholders are so divided that they have failed to elect successors to directors whose terms have expired or would have expired upon qualification of their successors`
         OR (    a's `the business of the corporation is suffering or is threatened with irreparable injury because the directors are so divided that the required vote for action by the board cannot be obtained`
             AND a's `the stockholders are unable to terminate that division`)
         OR (    a's `the corporation has abandoned its business`
             AND a's `the corporation has failed within a reasonable time to take steps to dissolve, liquidate or distribute its assets`))

-- "and, if the corporation is insolvent, to be receivers".
-- src:921 | (a) The Court of Chancery, upon application of any stockholder, may appoint 1 or more persons to be custodians, and, if the corporation is insolvent, to be receivers, of and for any corporation when:
@ref 8 Del. C. § 226(a) (src:921)
GIVEN a IS A `dg5 s 226(a) Application for a custodian`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 226(a) the Court of Chancery may appoint a receiver as well` a MEANS
        `s 226(a) a ground exists on which the Court of Chancery may appoint a custodian` a
    AND a's `the corporation is insolvent`

-- out of range: section 352(a)(2) (piece dg10)
-- out of range: section 291 (piece dg9)
-- The custodian has the powers and title of a receiver under section 291 (out of range, piece dg9), but the authority is to continue the business and not to liquidate,
-- "except when the Court shall otherwise order and except in cases arising under paragraph (a)(3) of this section or § 352(a)(2) of this title" (out of range: section 352(a)(2), piece dg10).
-- src:925 | (b) A custodian appointed under this section shall have all the powers and title of a receiver appointed under § 291 of this title, but the authority of the custodian is to continue the business of the corporation and not to liquidate its affairs and distribute its assets, except when the Court shall otherwise order and except in cases arising under paragraph (a)(3) of this section or § 352(a)(2) of this title.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 226(b) (src:925)
GIVEN `the Court has otherwise ordered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appointment arises under paragraph (a)(3) of section 226` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appointment arises under section 352(a)(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 226(b) the custodian's authority is to continue the business and not to liquidate its affairs` `the Court has otherwise ordered` `the appointment arises under paragraph (a)(3) of section 226` `the appointment arises under section 352(a)(2)` MEANS
        (NOT `the Court has otherwise ordered`)
    AND (NOT `the appointment arises under paragraph (a)(3) of section 226`)
    AND (NOT `the appointment arises under section 352(a)(2)`)

-- src:925 | A custodian appointed under this section shall have all the powers and title of a receiver appointed under § 291 of this title, but the authority of the custodian is to continue the business of the corporation and not to liquidate its affairs and distribute its assets, except when the Court shall otherwise order and except in cases arising under paragraph (a)(3) of this section or § 352(a)(2) of this title.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 226(b) (src:925)
GIVEN `the person is a custodian appointed under section 226` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 226(b) the custodian has all the powers and title of a receiver appointed under s 291` `the person is a custodian appointed under section 226` MEANS
    `the person is a custodian appointed under section 226`

-- "the applicant shall provide a copy of any application referred to in subsection (a) of this section to the Attorney General ... within 1 week of its filing with the Court of Chancery":
-- seven days after the filing date, the last day inside (Fork F3 in NOTES.md). NOTHING: the corporation is not a charitable nonstock corporation, so no such duty.
-- src:926 | (c) In the case of a charitable nonstock corporation, the applicant shall provide a copy of any application referred to in subsection (a) of this section to the Attorney General of the State of Delaware within 1 week of its filing with the Court of Chancery.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 226(c) (src:926)
GIVEN k IS A `Kind of corporation`
      `the date the application was filed with the Court of Chancery` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 226(c) the last day for the applicant to provide a copy to the Attorney General` k `the date the application was filed with the Court of Chancery` MEANS
    IF `the kind is a charitable nonstock corporation` k
    THEN JUST (`the date` (`period in weeks` 1) `after` `the date the application was filed with the Court of Chancery`)
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref 8 Del. C. § 226(c) (src:926)
GIVEN k IS A `Kind of corporation`
      `the date the application was filed with the Court of Chancery` IS A DATE
      `the date the applicant provided a copy to the Attorney General` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 226(c) the applicant provided the copy to the Attorney General in time` k `the date the application was filed with the Court of Chancery` `the date the applicant provided a copy to the Attorney General` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 226(c) the last day for the applicant to provide a copy to the Attorney General` k `the date the application was filed with the Court of Chancery`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST last THEN
        CONSIDER `the date the applicant provided a copy to the Attorney General`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST FALSE
        WHEN JUST d  THEN JUST (d AT MOST last)

§ `Section 227 -- powers of the Court in elections of directors`

-- src:930 | (a) The Court of Chancery, in any proceeding instituted under § 211, § 215 or § 225 of this title may determine the right and power of persons claiming to own stock to vote at any meeting of the stockholders.
-- src:931 | (b) The Court of Chancery may appoint a Magistrate in Chancery to hold any election provided for in § 211, § 215 or § 225 of this title under such orders and powers as it deems proper; and it may punish any officer or director for contempt in case of disobedience of any order made by the Court; and, in case of disobedience by a corporation of any order made by the Court, may enter a decree against such corporation for a penalty of not more than $5,000.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 227(a) (src:930); § 227(b) (src:931)
DECLARE `dg5 s 227 Proceeding in the Court of Chancery` IS ONE OF
    `a proceeding instituted under section 211`
    `a proceeding instituted under section 215`
    `a proceeding instituted under section 225`
    `a proceeding not instituted under section 211, 215 or 225`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 227(a) (src:930)
GIVEN p IS A `dg5 s 227 Proceeding in the Court of Chancery`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 227 the proceeding is one that section 227 reaches` p MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `a proceeding instituted under section 211` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a proceeding instituted under section 215` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a proceeding instituted under section 225` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a proceeding not instituted under section 211, 215 or 225` THEN FALSE

-- The Court may determine "the right and power of persons claiming to own stock to vote at any meeting of the stockholders".
@ref 8 Del. C. § 227(a) (src:930)
GIVEN p IS A `dg5 s 227 Proceeding in the Court of Chancery`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 227(a) the Court of Chancery may determine the right and power of a person claiming to own stock to vote` p MEANS
    `s 227 the proceeding is one that section 227 reaches` p

-- src:931 | The Court of Chancery may appoint a Magistrate in Chancery to hold any election provided for in § 211, § 215 or § 225 of this title under such orders and powers as it deems proper …
