`s 227(b) the Court of Chancery may punish the officer or director for contempt` `the officer or director disobeyed an order made by the Court` MEANS
    `the officer or director disobeyed an order made by the Court`

-- "in case of disobedience by a corporation of any order made by the Court, may enter a decree against such corporation for a penalty of not more than $5,000".
-- The amount is the Court's; the text states only the limit. NOTHING: the corporation has not disobeyed an order, so the text allows no such decree.
-- src:931 | and, in case of disobedience by a corporation of any order made by the Court, may enter a decree against such corporation for a penalty of not more than $5,000.
